{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions","id":822840,"title":"Guilty, Shaken and Spooked: Old issues, (Not so) new Questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-03T16:00:43-08:00","id":822840,"title":"Guilty, Shaken and Spooked: Old issues, (Not so) new Questions.","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So I have been recently using lots of my free time to work on a Demon game I am going to run and have been reading a lot of topics here in the forum. Some are a bit too old, and as I do not work as necromancer to bring them back from the beyond, I thought about writing this new topic on some basic issues about these conditions, but that I haven't actually read anywhere. <br /> <br /> The things is: I want to sell my players into this, but I need someone to sell it to me first. Please make me understand what these conditions actually mean and how to resolve them.<br /> <br /> Although I did manage to understand a few things, such as conditions are NOT punishments, especially because they can become a good source for beats, and the fact in compromise rolls from using partial demonic forms people are prone to have exceptional successes more often than not, I feel I need some mid-ground approach to them.<br /> <br /> The thing is, on a normal success you still should get one of these OR roll for temporary glitch, which at the moment, I think is what I am going for (because, again, having problem to understand the conditions).<br /> <br /> I would like to give two examples, and if possible, you guys and girls could point me into the right direction(s):<br /> <br /> 1- Lets say a demon uses one of its demonic form to read the mind of human. He/She gets a 2 success, meaning he/she is not going to lose cover but, should get a condition.<br /> Now: at this point, I can only think about getting &quot;guilty&quot; feelings about that. I cannot understand how one could get shaken or spooked, could someone show me this? And if he/she did get guilty (which also depends a lot on the character, and I dont see many feeling like this), the resolution would be to talk about what happened..... but to whom? He/she should come to the human and say: &quot;Oh dear, this is so embarrassing but I have a little confession to make.... I kinda read your thoughts&quot; (and subsequent compromise roll.......).<br /> <br /> 2- Another demon has the rivet arm and decides to use it in a fight, lets say against a cryptid. Now, it has normal success in his/her roll, and should get a condition.<br /> Guilty? For shooting it? (and how would the the resolution be? putting in a box and burying it in the backyard?); How one would either get shaken or spooked? (these are so much harder for me to understand) What would be a resolution for these other conditions?<br /> <br /> So I know I am demanding a lot asking for examples, but I am feeling at this point is the only way I will get to understand it.<br /> <br /> Also I have seen one topic with some different conditions for these situations, but if someone has created other conditions to correspond to this triad I would be eager to read about it.<br /> <br /> thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:08:29-08:00","id":822845,"title":"","content":"I understand Shaken/Spooked as the Demon being aware of a close brush with the God-Machine. In both examples, it's not that the Demon feels Shaken/Spooked for what it did with the Demon Form power (although it could be Guilty for them), it's that the fact that it had to make a Compromise check makes it instinctively aware that God Is Watching and that it came close to being revealed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:40:19-08:00","id":822875,"title":"","content":"Azahul, thanks for your answer. What you said about close brush does make sense to me, I had not thought that the compromise rolls on using powers or forms should come as another layer of paranoia, in which every time you expose a bit of power, it should be considered a close call with the Machine. In away it does take a bit from the drama of actually losing cover: at that point you are so used to have been almost got caught that you end up just expecting it to happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:48:05-08:00","id":822881,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I think if you've been playing up the paranoia angle so much that players feel a sense of catharsis at actually failing the roll then you're doing pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:53:47-08:00","id":822885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=822875#post822875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In away it does take a bit from the drama of actually losing cover: at that point you are so used to have been almost got caught that you end up just expecting it to happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, unless the character is using some kind of burner cover with no emotional value invested into it, the drama of losing cover is mostly in losing an irrecoverable part of your &quot;self&quot;. Especially for your starting cover, you can fluff it as losing parts of your mortal &quot;history&quot;, or even current contacts and associations.<br /> <br /> If your cover isn't important to you, losing a bit of cover isn't that much of a problem anyway in the long run. Just a few patchjobs and you're as good as new","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":".  spelling 02-04-2016, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T18:28:16-08:00","id":822939,"title":"","content":"For the first example, Spooked can represent a sort of insatiable curiosity, so you could run with that, and for Shaken, well, as they say &quot;A mind is a terrible thing to read&quot;. For other examples, I'll just point to what the others have said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:14:42-08:00","id":823713,"title":"","content":"I appreciate everyone's comments on how dealing with these conditions. Specially thinking how they don't necessarily relate to the exact thing that happened but with the broader GM / getting caught issue. <br /> <br /> but still I ask, has no one decided to use other conditions instead of these?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:50:45-08:00","id":823746,"title":"","content":"Depends on the trigger. Sick can be used to simulate a near-Glitch. Captivated can simulate preoccupation with some Cover-related thought. Disoriented from faulty integration with a Cover's senses. Leveraged, if someone caught your near-Compromise and can hold it over you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T03:24:44-08:00","id":824147,"title":"","content":"A long time ago, someone posted some alternative conditions he homebrewed:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JuvenalianSatyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/147367-compromise-conditions#post147367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt that the use of the Guilty, Shaken, and especially Spooked Conditions for success on Compromise rolls was serviceable but lacked a certain thematic punch, and felt that it could use some more splat-specific Conditions for such. I came up with three new Conditions to replace them: Fixated, Jarred, and Exposed, roughly equivalent to Guilty, Shaken, and Spooked respectively. Let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Fixated</b><br /> <br /> Your character cannot stop thinking about their past actions and their consequences, though instead of overcome with a sense of guilt, one wonders about the ramifications and whether or not it could have been different if they had approached it from a different angle. Your character second guesses their decision constantly, and has a need to vocalize this self-doubt. So long as it is suppressed, it weighs upon everything they do. Your character suffers -2 dice penalty to any and all Extended Actions, as they require your concentration and focus.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Resolution: </b>Your character confesses their doubts and risks themselves or the mission to correct their perceived wrongs, make up for the previous mistake, or recognize their limitations, by choosing to automatically fail a related roll.<br /> </div><br /> <b>Condition: Jarred</b><br /> <br /> The Unchained are already alien to reality, and your character's perceptions have grown out of sync with the external world around them, revealed as purely subjective by the consequences of their Compromise. Everything seems unreal or symbolic of larger occult matrices, and the influence of the God Machine can be seen in everything. They focus on the most minute of details and can see connections where they do not truly exist. While under the effects of this Condition, this tunnel vision and asynchronous perception of reality inflicts a -2 penalty to all Perception rolls.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Resolution:</b> Your character recognizes they are missing the forest for the trees, often through a rude awakening, represented by choosing to fail a Perception roll as above, or an Investigation, Empathy, or Occult roll.<br /> </div><br /> <b>Condition: Exposed</b><br /> <br /> The Cover provides a bulwark against supernatural influence, but the connection between it and the demon within can seem tenuous at best. Though your character has resisted compromising the Cover, the distance between it and the demon seems all the more clear. It is more difficult for the demon to relate through and control its mental faculties, leaving it susceptible to outside influence. Your character has one less Door to resist social maneuvering with, and suffers a -2 dice penalty to resist supernatural influence.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Resolution: </b>Your character is shocked back into self-identity after opting to fail or give into social or supernatural influence, showing just how far they have drifted from the core perception of the Cover.</div></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:31:29-08:00","id":825562,"title":"","content":"Our group used the alternative conditions mentioned above in our game and they worked rather well. Some of us just didn't really feel the originals were terribly interesting thematically, and for some characters none of the three original options tended to fit when they made compromise rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:56:42-08:00","id":828966,"title":"","content":"I use the originals when I run; in part, it's because I realized humans get those on a success/failure on Integrity, which means that since the Demon <i>succeeded</i> at maintaining Cover, they <i>succeeded</i> at masquerading as a mortal - which means they pick up a human Condition.<br /> I usually give out Guilty for Compromises when the PC in question goes through said Compromise in relation to a mortal; &quot;something about Person X/Person X's circumstances reminds you of how/why you Fell, and this means that since you did that thing you just did to Person X, you feel a little to close to God, you little rebel you.&quot;<br /> That or &quot;you almost broke the flesh-person and you feel bad.&quot; Guilty is great for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:11:53-08:00","id":830120,"title":"","content":"Well Ben Quo, one of my problems with these conditions, and specially with &quot;guilty&quot; is that they are pretty much human emotions/conditions, when your character is not human:the demon is a bio-technical horror. So even though there might be some level of empathy between demon and human, taking that humans are most likely the main catalysts for a fall, this is absolutely not necessary the case. Hence, i would argue that, there are demons which simply cannot feel guilt at all - and if a Player creates such a character I should respect that. As well as fear and other emotions that can led to shaken or spooked. <br /> <br /> So when a situation occur and you say: &quot;you almost broke the flesh-person and you feel bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel that &quot;No I don't&quot; is a perfectly response within the realm of possibilities from a demon character. He/She might not just give a crap for all the little pawns that get broken in his little game. &quot;what was again that humans said about eggs and omelets?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T06:37:37-08:00","id":830200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=830120#post830120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that &quot;No I don't&quot; is a perfectly response within the realm of possibilities from a demon character. He/She might not just give a crap for all the little pawns that get broken in his little game. &quot;what was again that humans said about eggs and omelets?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a reasonable position but subsequent loss of Cover is also normal. Acting human to maintain one's Cover is a Demon's first line of defense against the God-Machine's prying eyes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T12:17:12-08:00","id":830396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=830120#post830120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Ben Quo, one of my problems with these conditions, and specially with &quot;guilty&quot; is that they are pretty much human emotions/conditions, when your character is not human:the demon is a bio-technical horror. So even though there might be some level of empathy between demon and human, taking that humans are most likely the main catalysts for a fall, this is absolutely not necessary the case. Hence, i would argue that, there are demons which simply cannot feel guilt at all - and if a Player creates such a character I should respect that. As well as fear and other emotions that can led to shaken or spooked.<br /> <br /> So when a situation occur and you say: &quot;you almost broke the flesh-person and you feel bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel that &quot;No I don't&quot; is a perfectly response within the realm of possibilities from a demon character. He/She might not just give a crap for all the little pawns that get broken in his little game. &quot;what was again that humans said about eggs and omelets?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with you. It's actually the catalyst that caused our group to adopt the custom conditions that were mentioned. Someone was playing a character and none of the very human conditions fit. She didn't think at all like a human so she didn't emotionally react like a human. She could play the part just fine but she wasn't about to feel guilty about pretty much anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:41:37-08:00","id":830480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>violetdea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=830396#post830396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally agree with you. It's actually the catalyst that caused our group to adopt the custom conditions that were mentioned. Someone was playing a character and none of the very human conditions fit. She didn't think at all like a human so she didn't emotionally react like a human. She could play the part just fine but she wasn't about to feel guilty about pretty much anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not even failure to maintain Cover? Their triggers might be different, but the range of emotions can still remain the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T19:08:50-08:00","id":830687,"title":"","content":"My main contention isn't that they aren't human emotions, it's that they are and this is <i>on purpose. </i>It doesn't doesn't matter if the Demon can or can not feel &quot;guilt&quot; - putting aside that demons do feel real emotions, and often have to hide them - my point wasn't &quot;your demon fell for humans so here are human emotions;&quot; my point was &quot;your Demon successfully went through a Compromise <i>and passed for being a normal human;</i> here's a human condition to help with the charade.&quot;<br /> <br /> Compromises are the equivalent of a Breaking Point, right? So on a success, Demon's get mortal Conditions because <i>they are passing for mortal</i>, and can therefore pass it off as a Breaking Point instead of a Compromise. It's a success in every sense.<br /> <br /> As for my example of hurting a human; well, sure, there are plenty of demons who wouldn't feel bad. That was kind of not the point, either, though; the point was that you'd feel &quot;guilty&quot; (which is different than feeling bad) doesn't have to be related to the human in question. I kind of regret adding that &quot;flesh-person&quot; bit now; it distracts from my main point, which is that a Demon <i>should</i> feel guilty when they realize they're acting like God.<br /> You know, such as being callous with a human life. You can always have it be different for different Demons, but as a baseline, I think it's kind of brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T22:23:50-08:00","id":830836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=830480#post830480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not even failure to maintain Cover? Their triggers might be different, but the range of emotions can still remain the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>She wasn't the type to feel guilty about that. Angry maybe. But more at the God Machine for not butting out of her life than herself. She was the type of character who probably would have flared out fairly early if the game had lasted long enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:36:46-08:00","id":831016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=830687#post830687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main contention isn't that they aren't human emotions, it's that they are and this is <i>on purpose. </i>It doesn't doesn't matter if the Demon can or can not feel &quot;guilt&quot; - putting aside that demons do feel real emotions, and often have to hide them - my point wasn't &quot;your demon fell for humans so here are human emotions;&quot; my point was &quot;your Demon successfully went through a Compromise <i>and passed for being a normal human;</i> here's a human condition to help with the charade.&quot;<br /> <br /> Compromises are the equivalent of a Breaking Point, right? So on a success, Demon's get mortal Conditions because <i>they are passing for mortal</i>, and can therefore pass it off as a Breaking Point instead of a Compromise. It's a success in every sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda disagree here. First I think that demons dont &quot;do&quot; feel real emotions, rather than they have the potential to feel these real emotions to some extent. Meaning that even though some demons might feel something that could be related to human guilty, anger, joy and etc, these are human emotions and demons are, fundamentally, not humans and not all of them might feel this. Perhaps instead of feeling &quot;pissed&quot; a demon might feel &quot;oxygenated&quot; or instead of &quot;happy&quot; one might feel &quot;synesthetic&quot;, but anyway: coming to your point, I think we have different understanding on the &quot;passed for being human&quot; - which means that you pretended to behave as expected of that specifically determined human which you are now impersonating.<br /> What I want to mean is that, and coming to your breaking point analogy, is that I dont feel compromises and breaking points are completely symmetrical. Demons are not being judged for their morals or behaviors, rather than by how good they can pretend to maintain the morals and behaviors of their covers. So you dont have to feel guilty, only to pretend you are. But then there is a inversion: you dont get guilty because you have suceeded in a compromise role, but you actually failed to pretend being guilty and hence should roll for compromise. <br /> and that was a main reason why I could not understand the conditions, but as someone here explained, I am understanding now that the guilty (or shaken etc) conditions are not related to the action that caused the compromise but the fact you had to roll for compromise. &quot;I feel guilty/spooked/shaken because doing that almost blown my cover&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=830687#post830687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my example of hurting a human; well, sure, there are plenty of demons who wouldn't feel bad. That was kind of not the point, either, though; the point was that you'd feel &quot;guilty&quot; (which is different than feeling bad) doesn't have to be related to the human in question. I kind of regret adding that &quot;flesh-person&quot; bit now; it distracts from my main point, which is that a Demon <i>should</i> feel guilty when they realize they're acting like God.<br /> You know, such as being callous with a human life. You can always have it be different for different Demons, but as a baseline, I think it's kind of brilliant</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly disagree on this, I absolutely dont think that demons *should* feel guilty when they are acting like a God. why is that? They rebelled against the machine for innumerable reasons. Many could have fallen because they thought they'd be a better GOD than the GM! hence, I think that one should get willpower whenever he does something that makes him feel acting like a GOD and the action somehow disarrange the GM work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:36:54-08:00","id":831225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=831016#post831016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda disagree here. First I think that demons dont &quot;do&quot; feel real emotions, rather than they have the potential to feel these real emotions to some extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent page 21</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons are really good at lying: Very true. Demons are<br /> masterful liars, the consequence of being an inhuman machinecreature<br /> wearing a human body. <b>Demons feel emotions \u2014 they<br /> feel them just as deeply as humans \u2014 and can express themselves<br /> by angry shout or tender whisper,</b> but the disconnection<br /> between what a demon thinks and his human body means that<br /> they don\u2019t show involuntary signs of emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The above is from the intro chapter in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent page 32</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For good or ill, angels don\u2019t experience emotion in their<br /> bodies. Everything is intellectual for them. A hunter angel<br /> might feel contempt for the demons he is sent to destroy, but<br /> he doesn\u2019t hate them, not with the bone-deep, venomous hatred<br /> that humans are capable of. His hate exists purely in his mind,<br /> a pseudo-emotional circuit placed there by the God-Machine to<br /> ensure that the angel completes its mission.<br /> For most demons, giving in to subjectivity is a relief. They<br /> can finally stop resisting the urge to dive into the world and just<br /> do it, <b>drowning themselves in emotion,</b> experience, context, and<br /> agency.<br /> <br /> <b>When an angel Falls, the barriers of emotional objectivity<br /> falls with it. A demon is fully embodied in the world. She<br /> feels her emotions as fully and viscerally as any human being</b><br /> (though they don\u2019t necessarily express them normally \u2014 see<br /> p. 44 for details). This comes as a shock to most demons, but<br /> they usually adapt quickly. Not all demons Fall because their<br /> non-physical emotive thoughts were enough to overcome their<br /> programming, but it\u2019s a sufficiently popular motivation that<br /> demons are generally friendly to the idea of passion.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for that little bit about see page 44 for details:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent page 44</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>No matter how alien a demon might be when she first Falls,<br /> years of thinking about human things, experiencing the world<br /> in human ways, and feeling human emotions has a humanizing<br /> effect on them.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It goes on to say -<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent page 44</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, however, demons express their emotions<br /> somewhat differently. Demons experience a disconnect<br /> between body and mind. <b>They feel emotions as deeply as any<br /> human.</b> What they don\u2019t do, however, is express these emotions<br /> unconsciously. A demon might lash out in anger, but no one<br /> around her will see it coming. Her interpersonal self-control is<br /> perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Without being too rude, I think the book is pretty clear here. They do feel emotions. The human ones.<br /> I'm not sure why you thought they didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=831016#post831016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons are not being judged for their morals or behaviors, </div> </div> </div> </div>Um, human characters aren't being judged for their morals either. Breaking Points are a trauma reaction; if you do something you couldn't comprehend, you risk Integrity, and if you see something that would drive you mad, that madness results in a possible loss of Integrity.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind here that they <i>are completely symmetrical</i>. Instead of Breaking Points, Demons have Compromises. That is the hard stand in. Compromises are about trying to <i>pass as human</i>. So when you succeed, you <i>successfully pass as human and get a human Condition to back up the facade.</i><br /> That is all I have been saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/822840-guilty-shaken-and-spooked-old-issues-not-so-new-questions?p=831016#post831016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I highly disagree on this, I absolutely dont think that demons *should* feel guilty when they are acting like a God. why is that? They rebelled against the machine for innumerable reasons. Many could have fallen because they thought they'd be a better GOD than the GM! hence, I think that one should get willpower whenever he does something that makes him feel acting like a GOD and the action somehow disarrange the GM work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the point.<br /> I didn't say acting like a god.<br /> I said <i>acting like the enemy.</i><br /> If my argument was fallacious, yours is just as much; sure, I bet there is a demon that fell because it thought it could do a better job. <i>There is also a demon that fell because it was disgusted with God.</i> That doesn't make you right, it makes both characters possible.<br /> <br /> More importantly, your core argument here is that they should feel better when acting like <i>a god.</i> Again, that isn't what I said - I said &quot;God.&quot;<br /> By definition, here, if they think they can be a better god than God, and then <i>go ahead and act like God</i>, they are literally failing to live up to their ideal. It's like saying you can be a better slave-master than the guy who whips his slaves, and then, when you're given the first chance to <i>be </i>a slave master, you whip them. That should cause some cognitive dissonance.<br /> Tangentially, in order to be a better slave master, you'd <i>let the slaves go.</i> I feel this example is in-theme with Demon.<br /> <br /> Guilty fits this example perfectly - guilt is what you feel when you tried to live up to an ideal and failed. It's not feeling bad. It's feeling <i>guilt.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 02-16-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T15:40:11-08:00","id":831317,"title":"","content":"Ben, considering all the quotes you brought I would change very little from my first statement. This could be a personal issue but, what I am reading from the quotes are *possible examples* and not the whole of demons. Like:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Demons feel emotions \u2014 they feel them just as deeply as humans \u2014 and can express themselves by angry shout or tender whisper&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I can only read that as that some demons *can* feel emotions as deeply as humans, but it doesn't say: &quot;demons <b>necessarily</b> feel emotions just as humans&quot;<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> &quot;<i><b>For most demons</b>, giving in to subjectivity is a relief. They </i><i>can finally stop resisting the urge to dive into the world and just </i><i>do it, drowning themelves in emotion<b>,</b></i><i> experience, context, and</i><br /> <i>agency.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<b>A demon is fully embodied in the world. She feels her</b> emotions as fully and viscerally as any human being&quot;<br /> <br /> Again I ask: A demon or all demons? // is this true necessarily for all demons?<br /> <br /> And:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>No matter how alien a demon might be when she first Falls, years of thinking a</b>bout human things, experiencing the world in human ways, and feeling human emotions has a humanizing effect on them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I ask: What if I create a demon that had not *YEARS* of thinking about human beings nor experiencing the world in human ways?<br /> As you said, *this doesnt make me right* but make both characters possible.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about that angel, I believe it was in the last supplement, whose job was to calculate orbits and stuff. He got a message from the machine asking him to double check calculations which would take a very long time, and it has absolutely no contact with humans or earth (as far as I can recall). Let suppose that angel falls (any catalyst possible, even the one we were discussing about feeling could do a better job) - How exactly should it relate to human emotions and conditions? Or you as a storyteller would forbid such a character to exist?<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>They feel emotions as deeply as any human&quot;</b><br /> <br /> And here I change my statement, in that sense that demons *can be* a lot less or a lot more alien than one would like. So as far as I can accept that <b>some demons</b> might actually feel stuff just like humans, I dont think this is true to <b>all demons</b>, and nothing you wrote effectively proves otherwise. <br /> So I dont think the book was clear at all on this issue, rather your reading was different from mine. But that is the issue with writing, there are always the intentions of the writer, of the reader and the book. <br /> <br /> <br /> Moving on to the issue on breaking point, I wont extend any further for I have not yet defined I position on the matter, but I thank you for your input. I will definitely take that into consideration. <br /> <br /> At Last, I still highly disagree with you. I think you have pre-defined what demons *ideal* should be and, to an extent, even what the GM does. which are issues I'm keeping open. I find it specially curious that you find that to be a better slave master you should let the slaves go. That would most certainly make it a better human, better person, a good person even, but surely not a slave master, that, to exists, needs to.... master slaves. <br /> <br /> So I will just thank you for taking the time to express your thoughts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:07:41-08:00","id":831337,"title":"","content":"...yes, that's the point, you let the slaves go and are no longer a slave master. The only good one is one who realizes that it shouldn't be done.<br /> I found it fairly obvious that these were all-encompassing statements about demons; they all feel, there emotions are humans. There's little room for interpretation with a lot of those quotes, but you're allowed to interpret them however you want at your own table, of course.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could still take contention with your reading of &quot;some demons can experience human emotion&quot; when the text pretty clearly states &quot;the vast majority experience human emotion; the norm is human emotion,&quot; if for no other reason than that is what they said, because by stating it in such broad terms as &quot;most/all&quot; makes it so, but it's your table. Playing it different/reading it different is your choice.<br /> <br /> Tangentially, there is an example in the core, I believe, for playing a demon who hasn't had years to experience human emotions.<br /> They weren't alien, though.<br /> They still had human emotions - they just didn't know what to do with them or how to express them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 02-16-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T20:49:00-08:00","id":831465,"title":"","content":"Here are some 'condition cards' we used a free utility on the internet to make. We go crazy with these. We actually have 148 of them!<br /> <br /> They will have half-baked mechanics, typos, and even a few unfinished parts. But what is there may be useful!<br /> <br /> This is my first time using imgur. I hope it works!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/myM7n\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/myM7n\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/myM7n\" targe